-- akn:att_3__hc_1 Annex C, the form of a request to leave Ofek Hadash (section 11): its fields, the principal's comment and the address; the rule is section 11's.

§§ `נספח ד' קביעת דרגה והמרות שכר`

-- The opening: an existing teacher's grade is set by converting the
-- salary, by the teacher's data, roles and the stage employed in; a new
-- teacher is placed at grade 1 by education and role, without conversion;
-- the Ministry alone sets grades.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1/p1 akn:att_4__hc_1/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_3
GIVEN t IS A `teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the salary is converted` t IF
    `is an existing teacher` t

-- 1: the conversion for existing teachers: A = X × (100% + Y) / 100. X is
-- the salary for 100% by the roles in March of the year before joining
-- (combined salary, the supplements, and the role allowances that do not
-- continue); without employment in that March, the joining month; after
-- unpaid leave or a sabbatical that year, September's of the joining year.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p6 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p15 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p16 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p17 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_4
GIVEN X IS A NUMBER @desc the salary to convert
      Y IS A NUMBER @desc the conversion factor, as a fraction
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the converted salary` X Y IS
    X TIMES (1 PLUS Y)

DECLARE `month the salary is taken from` IS ONE OF
    `March of the year before joining`
    `the joining month`
    `September of the joining year`

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p6 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2
GIVEN `employed that March` IS A BOOLEAN, `on unpaid leave or sabbatical the year before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `month the salary is taken from`
DECIDE `the month for the salary to convert` `employed that March` `on unpaid leave or sabbatical the year before` IS
    IF `on unpaid leave or sabbatical the year before` THEN `September of the joining year`
    ELSE IF `employed that March` THEN `March of the year before joining`
         ELSE `the joining month`

-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p7 The letterhead repeated inside the annex; no rule.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p8 The letterhead repeated; no rule.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p9 The letterhead repeated; no rule.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p10 The letterhead repeated; no rule.

-- The factors for academic teachers (Y) are announced under this heading
-- and no table follows in the corpus (a corpus defect): Y is an input.
-- Non-academics (28 years and up): the academic factor × 0.8. Primary
-- school, grades 7-9 on the 24-hour base: the factor + 12.5% for that part,
-- taught on the primary week.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p11 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p12 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p13 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p14
GIVEN `academic factor` IS A NUMBER, academic IS A BOOLEAN, `grades 7-9 on the 24-hour base in primary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the teacher's conversion factor` `academic factor` academic `grades 7-9 on the 24-hour base in primary` IS
    LET base MEANS IF academic THEN `academic factor` ELSE `academic factor` TIMES 0.8
    IN  IF `grades 7-9 on the 24-hour base in primary` THEN base TIMES 1.125 ELSE base

-- A is placed in the table by education and seniority, at the grade whose
-- salary is the nearest one equal to or above it; and the 2016 shekel and
-- Ofek 2022 supplements are paid on top (1ב.5).
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p18 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_e akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_e/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p3
DECLARE `grade salary` HAS
    `table grade`        IS A NUMBER
    `grade's salary`     IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `converted amount` IS A NUMBER, `grade salaries` IS A LIST OF `grade salary` @desc the table's grades in ascending order, with their salaries for the teacher's education and seniority
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the grade the converted salary is placed at` `converted amount` `grade salaries` IS
    listToMaybe (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `table grade`)
                     (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `grade's salary` AT LEAST `converted amount`) `grade salaries`))

-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p19 The heading "דגשים"; its items follow.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2/p2 The heading "דגשים" repeated; the items after it (1ב.3, 1ב.4) repeat 1ב.1 and 1ב.2 word for word.

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_5
`the 2016 shekel and Ofek 2022 supplements are paid on the converted salary` MEANS TRUE

-- 2: first deputies: Y = 20%; X is the salary for 100% in March of the
-- year before, without the education allowance, reimbursements, sundry
-- payments, tax gross-up and imputed benefits (September's after leave).
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p3
`a first deputy's conversion factor` MEANS 0.2

-- 3: principals: Y = 15%, X likewise (without annual payments too).
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p3
`a principal's conversion factor` MEANS 0.15

-- X for a full position: the components paid for 100% as they are, the
-- components paid by the position scaled up to 100%.
GIVEN `paid for 100%` IS A NUMBER, `paid by the position` IS A NUMBER, `position factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary to convert at a full position` `paid for 100%` `paid by the position` `position factor` IS
    `paid for 100%` PLUS `paid by the position` DIVIDED BY `position factor`

-- The deputy example (2ג-2ה): an academic primary first deputy, position
-- factor 89.167%, complexity 8.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p6 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p7 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p8 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p9 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p10 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p11 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p12 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p13 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p14 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p15 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p16 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p17
`the deputy's components by the position` MEANS
    sum (LIST 4194.9, 139.91, 125.85, 207.83, 287.56, 155.58, 270.10, 567.2)

`the deputy's management allowance` MEANS 2143.92

#ASSERT `the deputy's components by the position` EQUALS 5948.93

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p18 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p19 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p20 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p21
`the deputy's X` MEANS
    `to the agora` (`the salary to convert at a full position` `the deputy's management allowance` `the deputy's components by the position` 0.89167)

#ASSERT `the deputy's X` EQUALS 8815.59

-- F-2025-26_tashpo_01-k: the example then multiplies X by 1.034, "תוספת
-- שחיקה", which neither the formula nor the definitions of X and Y name,
-- and converts 9,115.32 rather than X.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p22 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p23 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_d akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_d/p2
`the example's erosion factor` MEANS 1.034

`the deputy's A by the example` MEANS
    `to the agora` (`to the agora` (`the deputy's X` TIMES `the example's erosion factor`) TIMES (1 PLUS `a first deputy's conversion factor`))

#ASSERT `the deputy's A by the example` EQUALS 10938.38

`the deputy's A by the formula` MEANS
    `to the agora` (`the converted salary` `the deputy's X` `a first deputy's conversion factor`)

`the deputy example converts more than the formula gives` MEANS
    `the deputy's A by the example` GREATER THAN `the deputy's A by the formula`
#ASSERT `the deputy example converts more than the formula gives`

-- The deputy is placed at grade א', complexity 8: 17,716.63 for a full
